# Every pinned image and version, in one place (research.md R9, read 2026-09-28).
# Consumed by the Makefile, tests/run.sh and scan/scan.sh. Bump deliberately (tech-stack Guidelines).
# KEY=VALUE only: this file is sourced by bash and read by make.

DEBIAN_IMAGE=debian:trixie-slim@sha256:a99cfc517144bc59b1978475ec53b46ecabec7e43635402ee5b77cc54cd1b20a
# PYTHON_VERSION 3.14.8 fixes CVE-2026-19445 (critical) and CVE-2026-19553 (high) in 3.14.7 (lane 008s1-a, mentor ruling,
# feedback 06-20261009-162833 item 2). uv 0.12.19 to 0.12.21 offer CPython up to 3.14.7; 0.12.22 (2026-10-02) is the first
# stable uv whose download list has 3.14.8 (each release's `uv python list --only-downloads --offline`, read 2026-10-09).
# UV_IMAGE's digest is the image index's, read from ghcr.io on 2026-10-09.
UV_IMAGE=ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.12.22@sha256:f513a91fc62fe7c17567eee97230dd198e43edb8a9fbecca843714a4358fe1bc
PYTHON_VERSION=3.14.8

# The agent's runtimes (feature 007 slice 1, discovery revision 14; 007 spec FR-25): the agent Python is
# uv-managed CPython at PYTHON_VERSION in its own prefix; Node is the official tarball of the current
# Active LTS (24.x on 2026-10-08, read from nodejs.org/dist/index.json), checked against NODE_SHA256 from
# that release's SHASUMS256.txt in both the agent and vanilla builds (a mismatch fails the build).
NODE_VERSION=24.21.0
NODE_SHA256=6e1db87ef58b8819e5d5402eff1536491b18edd8eb7bee5ef7897876e88dc5ff
# npm itself, replacing the one Node 24.21.0 bundles (11.19.0), whose bundled ip-address, tar and
# brace-expansion carry fixable Highs (lane 007s1-a, item 3; the mentor's ruling, option 1). No Node 24.x
# release newer than 24.21.0 existed on 2026-10-08. 11.21.1 (published 2026-10-15T15:45:16Z) replaces
# 11.21.0: it ships brace-expansion 5.0.12 and undici 6.29.0, the fixes for the three Highs the scan named
# on 2026-10-15 (H9: a stable release of the bundling component inside the constraint, with no age rule;
# bridge/feedback/maint-20261015-195341-npm-advisories-scan-blocks.md). NPM_SHA512 is the registry's
# dist.integrity for npm-11.21.1.tgz (sha512, base64), written as hex for `sha512sum -c`, and checked
# against the tarball on 2026-10-15. The whole package goes in; nothing inside npm's tree is changed by hand.
NPM_VERSION=11.21.1
NPM_SHA512=613ccbe90044257c87713bb426251ced128ca7e9b3949b65eeb18b98445a5d441e14720c73d6ad76be86f4cf42f2f0d66efe347a9a13400ccd2f6fcfb5954385

# The speedup bench's live harnesses (feature 002 slice 1, FR-21 and FR-23; research RB12). Each is the native
# linux-x64 binary from its npm package, held in the bench's harness image and mounted read-only into task
# containers, never installed into an image under test. *_SHA512 is the registry's dist.integrity for the
# package tarball (sha512, base64), written as hex for `sha512sum -c`, and checked against the tarball on
# 2026-10-13: opencode-linux-x64@1.19.0 (published 2026-10-11) and @openai/codex@0.162.1-linux-x64 (2026-10-09).
OPENCODE_VERSION=1.19.0
OPENCODE_SHA512=f941719f601b3aa284212043aab5a4e671ec66b3d604c559e07f51eed6e7aedd7e9d8bc419e8e983db72b7e40cae904f6193fb17e0f7626d2f65b65c17b8124b
CODEX_VERSION=0.162.1
CODEX_SHA512=7232b699d1c87c47a9675950d4c5f7693402fbc9dc22cbe769c97feaf23674821c7cff3f32b853436faa46591714d0f32528f5777eaab88b333fedffe0250959
# The model both harnesses run (the operator's decision, 2026-10-12; FR-27: a dated id, never an alias), and its
# base price in USD per million tokens as OpenRouter's /api/v1/models listed it on 2026-10-13 (cheaper at listed
# UTC hours; the plan's estimate uses the base price). Spend recorded is OpenRouter's own figure, never these.
BENCH_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813
BENCH_MODEL_PRICE_IN=1.32
BENCH_MODEL_PRICE_OUT=3.96
# The date those two prices were read, printed with the plan's estimate so the operator can check its basis
# (Item 25's ruling, bridge/feedback/02-20261013-071257-item-25-the-relay-holds-the-key.md).
BENCH_MODEL_PRICE_READ=2026-10-13

BATS_IMAGE=bats/bats:1.14.0@sha256:5322b877351fda0cc435de8c6116de7d0a2ec79d7c680132a0ef329a633bc66f
# DOCKER_CLI_IMAGE: 29.9.0 (2026-10-09), the newest docker CLI release, and the first built with Go 1.26.9,
# which fixes GO-2026-6603 to -6613 (lane 005s1-a, item 3b; 29.8.1 and 29.8.2 are go1.26.8). The Go version
# was read on 2026-10-10 from the Go build info of /usr/local/bin/docker in the linux/amd64 image, pulled
# from the registry by this digest; the lane checks it with docker version --format '{{.Client.GoVersion}}'.
DOCKER_CLI_IMAGE=docker:29.9.0-cli@sha256:1a4c7cb63513f349bdad01fcc6e0f3f2f67d37b9da86f14dc0d4a0942eecda00
SHELLCHECK_IMAGE=koalaman/shellcheck:v0.11.0@sha256:61862eba1fcf09a484ebcc6feea46f1782532571a34ed51fedf90dd25f925a8d

SYFT_IMAGE=anchore/syft:v1.52.0@sha256:500e2d872ac019436926e8322b4fc1f39441d94d21f6f4046c6ff29b30e8cb02
GRYPE_IMAGE=anchore/grype:v0.119.0@sha256:8c2c9234a345577a6d321a4753aa3ee1276d8975c8452d2344a56b57733ecad3
GITLEAKS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/gitleaks/gitleaks:v8.30.1@sha256:c00b6bd0aeb3071cbcb79009cb16a60dd9e0a7c60e2be9ab65d25e6bc8abbb7f
PIP_AUDIT_VERSION=2.10.1

RUFF_VERSION=0.16.9
MYPY_VERSION=2.3.1
PYTEST_VERSION=8.4.2
# The unit step's workers (UNIT_JOBS > 1; maint-lane-speed part 1b): pytest-xdist and the execnet it runs on,
# fetched by the pinned uv as pytest is. pytest-xdist 3.8.0 (2025-07-01) needs pytest >= 7 and execnet >= 2.1.
PYTEST_XDIST_VERSION=3.8.0
EXECNET_VERSION=2.1.2

# Adele (feature 004): Go builder image (index digest, read 2026-10-09: Go 1.27.2 fixes nine stdlib
# advisories govulncheck reports reachable on 1.27.1), Go lint and vulnerability tools.
# STATICCHECK_VERSION is the module version of honnef.co/go/tools (release 2026.2.1 = v0.8.1).
GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27.2-trixie@sha256:e58d6f83b3416618d8bcac2b3dde1b7f7e3c4a77d25e88637f8bbae81536c48d
STATICCHECK_VERSION=v0.8.1
# GO_LINT_IMAGE runs staticcheck only (make lint), at GO_IMAGE's previous pin: staticcheck v0.8.1, the newest
# release, cannot import Go 1.27.2's export data (version 5; it reads up to 4). gofmt and go vet stay on GO_IMAGE.
# Nothing built here ships. Remove when a staticcheck release whose x/tools reads Go 1.27.2's export data
# exists: then staticcheck goes back to GO_IMAGE and this line is deleted (mentor ruling, feedback
# 04-20261009-010500 § Amendment 2026-10-09T01:40Z).
GO_LINT_IMAGE=golang:1.27.1-trixie@sha256:3b77fc618ec235a1ab412de7737f120dd507c57e8d87de4cbb7994fb94275ed5
GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=v1.8.0

# edit's syntax check (feature 008 slice 1; research R9): tree-sitter's Python binding and three prebuilt grammar
# wheels, installed into timelike's own interpreter (never the agent's, never the vanilla image) with
# --require-hashes --no-deps --only-binary. Each _SHA256 is the hash PyPI publishes for the exact wheel the build
# fetches, checked on 2026-10-09 against pypi.org/pypi/<name>/<version>/json. TREE_SITTER_SHA256 is the cp314
# manylinux x86_64 wheel's, so it moves with PYTHON_VERSION's minor version; the grammars are abi3 (cp39/cp310).
# Python and shell need nothing here: timelike's interpreter's compiler and /bin/bash -n check them.
TREE_SITTER_VERSION=0.26.0
TREE_SITTER_SHA256=f665510f0fcf4636fb9696f1f7853bed7a3bd764b7bb0cb8494e619c14ed5a0c
TREE_SITTER_TYPESCRIPT_VERSION=0.23.2
TREE_SITTER_TYPESCRIPT_SHA256=e96d36b85bcacdeb8ff5c2618d75593ef12ebaf1b4eace3477e2bdb2abb1752c
TREE_SITTER_GO_VERSION=0.25.0
TREE_SITTER_GO_SHA256=04b3b3cb4aff18e74e28d49b716c6f24cb71ddfdd66768987e26e4d0fa812f74
TREE_SITTER_RUST_VERSION=0.24.2
TREE_SITTER_RUST_SHA256=e033c5a93b57c88e0a835880de39fc802909ff69f57aaff6000211c196ea5190
